        "A response is that these texts show that people continue beyond bodily death, which few deny. They do not settle whether that continuance is a natural property of the soul or a gift held in being by God. Since Scripture says God ‘alone has immortality’, many conclude that all life, including any life after death, depends moment by moment on him. This is a debated question, and Christians of good faith land in different places."
